💬 Real-life conversation
You spontaneously tried to explain what you’d do if money weren’t an issue. That gave us several useful repairs.

You ultimately produced:

Esa es una buena pregunta. ✅

Probablemente viajaría a algún lugar nuevo, quizá a Europa porque nunca he viajado allí. ✅

You learned/reinforced:

viajaría = I would travel
viajará = he/she will travel
viajó = he/she traveled
he viajado = I have traveled
And you personally repaired:

Nunca he viajado allí. ✅

Then we worked on a new conditional structure:

¿Qué harías si no tuvieras que preocuparte por dinero? ✅

Important pattern:

si + imperfect subjunctive → conditional

Si no tuvieras que preocuparte… ¿qué harías?
= If you didn’t have to worry… what would you do?

That’s a useful step beyond memorized phrases because you’re beginning to build hypothetical thoughts yourself.

